## Static API/call findings

Repository and dependency input copies plus hashes are under inputs/, initial-bound-inputs.json and static-dependency-inputs.json. They were read as text/bytes; no compiler dependency was imported.

| Actual location | Finding / consequence |
| --- | --- |
| reporter.ts:9,61,79,82,101,116,120 | Default fs object; `writeFileSync(join(buildLogFolder,'log'), JSON.stringify(messages))`, no options; top-level `mkdirSync(buildLogFolder)`, no options. Both catch. createReporter(id?) has no supported disable/logDir option. End/error may write more than once. |
| compilation.ts:32,57,96 | Top-level default createReporter(); createCompile options are build/emitError/transpileOnly/preserveEnglish/noEmit. createCompile pipeline ends in reporter.end; no injection/disable option. |
| compilation.ts generator/task definitions | Monaco/enums and codicon source writes belong to separate task functions. createCompile entry does not invoke compileTask. Definitions/registrations are not task execution. |
| util.ts:342,369–373 | ensureDir uses mkdirSync; streamToPromise resolves on end or rejects on error. |
| tsb/index.ts:121 and transpiler.ts:303,367 | Actual ESBuildTranspiler uses async esbuild.transform on Vinyl Buffer, waits join then ends output. Other Tsc/transformSync branches are not claimed as actual writers. |
| graceful-fs.js:96 | Clones fs before its own patches; installation must precede gulp/TypeScript/es imports, not merely patch later. syncBuiltinESMExports covers builtin named exports; promises and FileHandle methods are separately guarded. |
| vinyl-fs/file-operations.js:240–275,331,338 | Destination uses open→write and fd metadata APIs (fchmod/futimes/possible fchown), not just writeFile. Path and fd mutation coverage is necessary. |
| esbuild/main.js:737,748,774,1760–1778,1978,2095 | codeFS/mapFS response branches exist. Input-temp threshold is >1MiB; current input81721 is below it. Native service is independent of Node fs hooks. Zip/PnP binary extraction can mkdir/copy/chmod node_modules; fixed ordinary Linux binary resolution excludes that branch. |

Native esbuild0.27.2 binary is 11100344 bytes / `ecd2aeff7d78a9feefa96d9c6f3bb9a9cbb38cc74ec3e7f044e8e6ed02e33d00`, pinned at ordinary `node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild`. Parent removes inherited ESBUILD_BINARY_PATH/preloads/compile-cache controls, uses ESBUILD_WORKER_THREADS=0, and gives each stage a unique TMPDIR/TMP/TEMP/XDG cache/config/data. This does **not** prove Go never creates temporary files: codeFS/mapFS rules are not reverse-engineered here. The service remains owned/monitored until cleanup, and poststream plus poststage full guards are mandatory. Node hooks are a controlled instrumentation layer, not a native-process security sandbox.

