## Parent WAL order and time evidence

Original Astra protocol-choice narrow review was forwarded by root as reviewer text (direct-message provenance, not terminal raw), C0/I0/M0 with conditions; root accepted it as §3.3/§4 implementation refinement, not a new-tool pass. Parent-authoritative WAL is permitted; concrete source review remains pending.

1. Child finishes real stream/destination and all source/output/seal checks, anchors one local hrtime duration, writes unique request ID+nonce and its actual PID/start/token/phase/path/bytes/SHA. Request/proposal and parent replies publish complete fsynced temporary bytes through an atomic no-replace hardlink plus directory fsync; only narrow private child publication capabilities may mutate those two control paths. Root static review found and corrected the earlier exists-before-full-write race; pre-correction sources and attribution remain under derivation/intermediate/control-publication-before. Request/proposal files are exclusive; proposal grants no write or restoration qualification.
2. Parent independently verifies actual owned exact emitter writer command/PID/start/token. A separate owned guard process checks the full fixed protections while the original parent monitor keeps scanning child/descendants and the **same** deadline. Its compact result binds the complete raw guard evidence hash.
3. Parent creates durable grant, fsyncs file+directory, then samples actual completion before the original deadline. It retains authoritative grant in memory and durable parent event, before publishing grant-ready. No child file can supply or overwrite the parent memory authority.
4. Child binds exact grant and proposes intent. Parent verifies proposal, same real grant, unrevoked stage, writer identity, fresh bytes and deadline. Parent appends **the true intent** to the unique WAL, fsyncs file+directory, and only **after completion** samples the parent's monotonic_ns. It is valid only if actual completion is before deadline. This is the single consumption.
5. Parent actual journal appender is separately recorded (`recordWriterPid/start/role=parent-authoritative-WAL`); the child actual out writer has its own PID/start/token. The parent durable authority event crosschecks intent full bytes/hash and grant. If validity cannot be proved, no ACK is issued; raw uncertainty is preserved.
6. ACK only references that same intent/permit/request/writer/hash. It does not consume again and is never a recovery eligibility requirement. Child verifies its complete journal bytes and parent identity. It uses **the same request anchor** against the parent remaining-duration value, subtracting *all* elapsed time since before request, which further tightens budget and never compares clock epochs. It cannot use a later ACK to reset its timer. Parent PID/start/nonzombie, revocation and failure-marker checks continue; the hook rechecks immediately before the captured write.
7. Sole Reveal hook validates seal and exact fresh bytes, increments once, records hook evidence, rechecks parent/budget, and uses the private captured open/writeSync complete-buffer/close capability with original writeFileSync default write semantics. Ordinary fs APIs cannot mutate out or erase the protected control/WAL/marker. Completion is emitted once by child, references the exact same permit/intent hash, and has an honest child recordWriter identity.
8. Parent revokes before cleanup; every outcome stops/reaps all owned descendants under nonrenewable TERM5/KILL5, including native service/guard process. Independent restoration reads real parent authority memory+durable records, actual qualified spawn/outWriter, full guard evidence hash and trusted journal prefix. Later expiry/end/revocation/ACK loss never cancels an already valid intent's recovery subset.

The regular watchdog is not a hard real-time kernel deadline. Parent full-tree guard runs out of process and cannot synchronously occupy the monitor; small protocol/file/fsync operations can still take time, and their **actual completion** is checked. No deadline or budget is renewed. Child conservative relative checks prevent cached late ACK from restarting execution even when original monitor already stopped/revoked; process cleanup remains required before restoration.

| Interruption point | Write/recovery classification |
| --- | --- |
| request/proposal only | no trusted intent, no out capability, no recovery authority |
| grant or WAL durability/validity cannot be proved before original deadline | no ACK, no out capability; preserve protocol uncertainty, no invented valid intent |
| valid parent intent durable, ACK missing/late | recovery eligibility retained; child cannot write without valid same-anchor ACK; unchanged bytes/mode/mtime cause no restoration write |
| ACK received, before out | eligibility retained; unchanged native remains untouched |
| out begun, error/partial/missing completion | valid intent + real grant/spawn/trusted prefix permits only Reveal partial/uncertain recovery after all owned quiet |
| exact completed | same permit/intent, exact fresh bytes and child completion qualify only Reveal recovery |
| later expiry/revocation/end | does not retroactively erase any preceding valid intent |

